method (LFMM, pcadapt, BayPass XtX, ...), but it treats a cluster's SNPs as
independent draws and is therefore anti-conservative in magnitude for large
correlated blocks (e.g. inversions). \code{"permutation"} re-runs an EMMAX scan on
the candidates under permuted phenotypes (requires \code{Y} and \code{K}); it captures
